From: be7000-openwrt <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: qca808x: enable the QCA8084 package clocks before touching its config registers

qca8084_phy_package_config_init_once() writes WORK_MODE_CFG and
EPHY_CFG, both in the chip's security-control block, and only then
enables the package clocks, among them nss_cc_sec_ctrl_ahb_clk that
feeds that block. Nothing else holds that clock, so clk_disable_unused()
gates it at about 2 s, long before the PHY package is configured at
about 12 s, and the two writes go nowhere.

Seen on a Xiaomi BE7000 whose QCA8084 never brings the 10GBASE-R link
to the SoC up: hours after boot WORK_MODE_CFG still read 0x3f, the reset
default with the switch-mode bit set, instead of the 0x2f the driver had
written, and the EPHY_CFG efuse-load bits were still set.

Enable the package clocks first.

diff --git a/drivers/net/phy/qcom/qca808x.c b/drivers/net/phy/qcom/qca808x.c
index 57034f7..c766173 100644
--- a/drivers/net/phy/qcom/qca808x.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/qcom/qca808x.c
@@ -1126,6 +1126,18 @@ static int qca8084_phy_package_config_init_once(struct phy_device *phydev)
 	int ret, mode;
 
 	shared_priv = phy_package_get_priv(phydev);
+
+	/* The work mode and EPHY_CFG registers below sit in the security
+	 * control block, clocked by nss_cc_sec_ctrl_ahb_clk. Nothing holds
+	 * that clock before this point, so clk_disable_unused() has gated it
+	 * by the time we get here and the writes are dropped: on a failing
+	 * BE7000 the work mode still read the reset default (0x3f, switch
+	 * bit set) long after this ran. Enable the package clocks first.
+	 */
+	ret = qca8084_package_clock_init(shared_priv);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	switch (shared_priv->package_mode) {
 	case QCA808X_PCS1_10G_QXGMII_PCS0_UNUNSED:
 		mode = QCA8084_WORK_MODE_QXGMII;
@@ -1182,10 +1194,7 @@ static int qca8084_phy_package_config_init_once(struct phy_device *phydev)
 			phydev_info(phydev, "QXGMII XPCS set up without BaseR lock, will redo it on first link up\n");
 	}
 
-	/* Initialize the PHY package clock and reset, which is the
-	 * necessary config sequence after GPIO reset on the PHY package.
-	 */
-	return qca8084_package_clock_init(shared_priv);
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static int qca8084_config_init(struct phy_device *phydev)
